IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sga1-sixth-schedule`

-- Tests for sga1-sixth-schedule.l4 (the Sixth Schedule). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion.

§ `Sixth Schedule, Part 1`

-- the 31 rows of the form (the rendering numbers none; the rows are numbered in the order of the rendering)
#ASSERT count `sch 6 Part 1 all the rows of the form` EQUALS 31

-- Arguments: the row; the share capital is divided into different classes; the statement is lodged by a private company on becoming a public company.
-- Every row the form lists is one the statement must state, except that row 5 depends on classes and rows 30 and 31 on a private company becoming public.
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 1 the issued share capital of the company and the shares it is divided into`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 2 the amount of the capital that consists of redeemable preference shares`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 3 the date on or before which the redeemable preference shares are, or are liable, to be redeemed`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 4 the names, descriptions and addresses of the directors or proposed directors`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- row 5: "If the share capital of the company is divided into different classes of shares"
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 5 where the share capital is divided into different classes, the voting rights and the rights in respect of capital and dividends of each class`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 5 where the share capital is divided into different classes, the voting rights and the rights in respect of capital and dividends of each class`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 6 the number and amount of shares and debentures issued in the 2 preceding years, or proposed or agreed to be issued, as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 7 the consideration for the issue or intended issue of those shares and debentures`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 8 the number, description and amount of the shares or debentures under option`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 9 the period during which the option is exercisable`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 10 the price to be paid for shares or debentures subscribed for or acquired under option`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 11 the consideration for the option or right to option`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 12 the persons to whom the option or right to option was given`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 13 the names and addresses of the vendors of property purchased or acquired, or proposed to be`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 14 the amount payable to each separate vendor`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 15 the amount paid or payable for any such property, specifying the amount for goodwill`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 16 short particulars of any transaction relating to such property completed within the 2 preceding years in which a vendor, promoter, director or proposed director had an interest`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 17 the amount paid or payable as commission for subscribing or procuring subscriptions, or the rate of the commission`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 18 the amount or rate of brokerage`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 19 the number of shares which persons have agreed for a commission to subscribe absolutely`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 20 the amount or estimated amount of preliminary expenses`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 21 by whom those expenses have been paid or are payable`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 22 the amount paid or intended to be paid to any promoter`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 23 the consideration for the payment to the promoter`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 24 any other benefit given or intended to be given to any promoter`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 25 the consideration for giving the benefit`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 26 the dates of, parties to, and general nature of every material contract`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 27 the time and place at which the contracts or copies may be inspected`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 28 the names and addresses of the auditors of the company`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 29 the nature and extent of the interest of every director and every expert in the promotion or in the property proposed to be acquired`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- row 30: "in the case of a statement to be lodged by a private company on becoming a public company"
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 30 the rates of the dividends paid in each of the 3 preceding financial years, or since incorporation if shorter`) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 30 the rates of the dividends paid in each of the 3 preceding financial years, or since incorporation if shorter`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- row 31: "in the case of a statement to be lodged by a private company on becoming a public company"
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 31 the cases in which no dividends have been paid on any class of shares in any of those years`) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the matter must be stated in the statement` (`sch 6 Part 1 row 31 the cases in which no dividends have been paid on any class of shares in any of those years`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Row 13: "except where the contract ... was entered into in the ordinary course of the business intended to be carried on by the company or the amount of the purchase money is not material".
-- Arguments: entered into in the ordinary course; the amount of the purchase money is not material.
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 row 13 the vendor's name and address must be stated` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 row 13 the vendor's name and address must be stated` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 row 13 the vendor's name and address must be stated` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 row 13 the vendor's name and address must be stated` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Row 26: "every material contract (other than contracts entered into in the ordinary course ... or entered into more than 2 years before the delivery of this statement)".
-- Arguments: the contract is material; entered into in the ordinary course; entered into more than 2 years before the delivery.
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 row 26 the contract must be stated as a material contract` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 row 26 the contract must be stated as a material contract` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 row 26 the contract must be stated as a material contract` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 row 26 the contract must be stated as a material contract` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Row 29: deemed indirect interest in a corporation. Arguments: beneficial interest in a corporation that has an interest in the promotion or property; in a corporation deemed related by s 6.
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 row 29 the director or expert is deemed to have an indirect interest in the corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 row 29 the director or expert is deemed to have an indirect interest in the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 row 29 the director or expert is deemed to have an indirect interest in the corporation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The statement states every matter the Part requires. Arguments: the matters stated; classes; a private company becoming public.
`all rows except those three` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN m YIELD    (NOT (m EQUALS `sch 6 Part 1 row 5 where the share capital is divided into different classes, the voting rights and the rights in respect of capital and dividends of each class`))
                         AND (NOT (m EQUALS `sch 6 Part 1 row 30 the rates of the dividends paid in each of the 3 preceding financial years, or since incorporation if shorter`))
                         AND (NOT (m EQUALS `sch 6 Part 1 row 31 the cases in which no dividends have been paid on any class of shares in any of those years`))) `sch 6 Part 1 all the rows of the form`

`all rows except row 7` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN m YIELD NOT (m EQUALS `sch 6 Part 1 row 7 the consideration for the issue or intended issue of those shares and debentures`)) `sch 6 Part 1 all the rows of the form`

`all rows except row 5` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN m YIELD NOT (m EQUALS `sch 6 Part 1 row 5 where the share capital is divided into different classes, the voting rights and the rights in respect of capital and dividends of each class`)) `sch 6 Part 1 all the rows of the form`

`all rows except row 31` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN m YIELD NOT (m EQUALS `sch 6 Part 1 row 31 the cases in which no dividends have been paid on any class of shares in any of those years`)) `sch 6 Part 1 all the rows of the form`

#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the statement states every matter the Part requires` `all rows except those three` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the statement states every matter the Part requires` `sch 6 Part 1 all the rows of the form` TRUE TRUE
-- a required row left out
#ASSERT (NOT `sch 6 Part 1 the statement states every matter the Part requires` `all rows except row 7` FALSE FALSE)
-- row 5 is required only if the capital is divided into classes
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the statement states every matter the Part requires` `all rows except row 5` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT `sch 6 Part 1 the statement states every matter the Part requires` `all rows except row 5` TRUE FALSE)
-- rows 30 and 31 are required (so a statement that omits one fails) only for a private company becoming a public company
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the statement states every matter the Part requires` `all rows except row 31` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT `sch 6 Part 1 the statement states every matter the Part requires` `all rows except row 31` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 1 the statement states every matter the Part requires` EMPTY FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Sixth Schedule, Part 2`

-- paragraph 1: "Where it is proposed to acquire a business or limited liability partnership"
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 1 a report is required` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 1 a report is required` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Arguments: by a public accountant appointed as auditor; named in the statement; the number of financial years of profits or losses given; the number the paragraph requires; assets and liabilities at the last date.
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 1 the report has the content the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE 3 3 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 1 the report has the content the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE 4 3 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 1 the report has the content the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE 2 3 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 1 the report has the content the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE 2 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 1 the report has the content the paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE 3 3 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 1 the report has the content the paragraph requires` TRUE FALSE 3 3 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 1 the report has the content the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE 3 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- paragraph 2(1)
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) a report is required` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) a report is required` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Arguments: by a public accountant appointed as auditor; named; deals with the other corporation under (2) or (3); indicates how profits would have concerned members; indicates the allowance for holders of other shares.
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) the report has the content the sub-paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) the report has the content the sub-paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) the report has the content the sub-paragraph requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) the report has the content the sub-paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) the report has the content the sub-paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(1) the report has the content the sub-paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) Arguments: the other corporation has no subsidiaries; the years of profits or losses dealt with; the years required; assets and liabilities dealt with at the last date.
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(2) the report deals with the other corporation as the sub-paragraph requires` TRUE 3 3 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(2) the report deals with the other corporation as the sub-paragraph requires` TRUE 2 3 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(2) the report deals with the other corporation as the sub-paragraph requires` TRUE 3 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(2) the report deals with the other corporation as the sub-paragraph requires` FALSE 3 3 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3)(a) Arguments: the other corporation has subsidiaries; deals separately as (2) provides; subsidiaries as a whole; subsidiaries individually; instead, as a whole with the other corporation.
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(a) the report deals with profits and losses as the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(a) the report deals with profits and losses as the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(a) the report deals with profits and losses as the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(a) the report deals with profits and losses as the paragraph requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(a) the report deals with profits and losses as the paragraph requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(a) the report deals with profits and losses as the paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3)(b) Arguments: the other corporation has subsidiaries; deals separately; subsidiaries as a whole (with or without the other corporation); subsidiaries individually.
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(b) the report deals with assets and liabilities as the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(b) the report deals with assets and liabilities as the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(b) the report deals with assets and liabilities as the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(b) the report deals with assets and liabilities as the paragraph requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3)(b) the report deals with assets and liabilities as the paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3) the report indicates the allowance for persons other than members of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 para 2(3) the report indicates the allowance for persons other than members of the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the Note
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 Note a statement that no report is required, with the reasons, should be furnished` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 2 Note a statement that no report is required, with the reasons, should be furnished` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Sixth Schedule, Part 3`

-- paragraph 3: "vendor" includes a vendor for the purposes of the repealed Fifth Schedule; "financial year" has the meaning in Part 3 of that Schedule
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 3 "vendor" the person is within the word vendor` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 3 "vendor" the person is within the word vendor` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 3 "financial year" the period is a financial year` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 3 "financial year" the period is a financial year` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- paragraph 4: less than 3 years and accounts for 2 years or one year only: 2 or 1 replaces 3
-- Arguments: carrying on business for less than 3 years; the number of years for which accounts have been made up.
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 4 the number of financial years a report must deal with` FALSE 3 EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 4 the number of financial years a report must deal with` TRUE 2 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 4 the number of financial years a report must deal with` TRUE 1 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 4 the number of financial years a report must deal with` TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 4 the number of financial years a report must deal with` TRUE 3 EQUALS NOTHING
-- paragraph 5. Arguments: indicates by way of note; makes the adjustments; indicates that adjustments have been made.
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 5 the report deals with adjustments as the paragraph requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 5 the report deals with adjustments as the paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 5 the report deals with adjustments as the paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 5 the report deals with adjustments as the paragraph requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 6 Part 3 para 5 the report deals with adjustments as the paragraph requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
